{"content":[{"c":["POTIPHERA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Priest of On whose daughter, Asenath, was given to Joseph as his wife by Pharaoh (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.41.45,50","r":"Gen.41.45,50","rawR":"Gen.41.45,50","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.41.45,50","value":"Gen.41.45,50"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 41:45, 50"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.20","r":"Gen.46.20","rawR":"Gen.46.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.20","value":"Gen.46.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"46:20"},"). On (or Heliopolis) was the center of the sun-god cult, and Potiphera was likely a high-ranking priest in the cult. His name, which means “he whom Re [the son god] has given,” does not appear in Egyptian records until the tenth century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", a fact employed by those who prefer a late date for the book of Genesis. Yet the name is known from the 15th century (the time of Moses), and its full form may be a modernization of a name common in Joseph’s era (20th century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=EgyptEgyptian_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"EgyptEgyptian_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"EgyptEgyptian_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Egypt, Egyptian"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Joseph_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Joseph_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Joseph_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Joseph #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Potiphera","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 41:45, 50","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.41.45,50","rawQueryValue":"Gen.41.45,50","sourceRefExact":"Gen.41.45,50"},{"anchorText":"46:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.20","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.20","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.20"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cc4de1fbd07eb75ec33f18a76b40a20b6d718a4589c16385826beb500c54582c","sourceItemName":"Potiphera","sourceItemOrder":247,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Potiphera","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Potiphera","title":"Potiphera","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}